From 4c878d452a4608da7b4aa80848ab1edfecca5d51 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Han <danielhanchen@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 21:26:02 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] CUDA: add IQ1_M to MMQ

IQ1_M weights are w = d*(2*s+1)*(g + delta) with g in {-1,0,1}, a 3 bit
sub-scale s per 16 values and delta = +-1/8 per 8 values. The delta is folded
into the int8 tile values (8*g +- 1 in {-9,-7,-1,1,7,9}) and the per-16 scale
becomes d*(2*s+1)/8, which is exact. The tile then uses the same Q8_0_16 data
layout and vec_dot (DP4A and MMA) as IQ2_XS, with D4 q8_1 activations.

Adds test-backend-ops coverage for IQ1_M/IQ1_S MUL_MAT and MUL_MAT_ID with
many experts, and perf cases for 1-bit MoE up projections.
---
